  "caption": "Quinn found a shoulder knot, squashed it with a massage ball, and two days later it was back.\n\nMuscle knots are probably not lumps you can break up. They're more likely areas of sensitive tissue and nerves. Massage or pressure can ease them for a while, but daily habits often decide whether they keep coming back.\n\nThings that often help: changing position often, protecting sleep and managing stress, building strength in the neck, shoulders and hips and keeping it going, and enjoying massage for comfort alongside movement.\n\nNight pain that doesn't ease with moving, fever, unexplained weight loss, or numbness or weakness should be checked by your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
